      "id": "inherited_unit:004.paragraph",
      "kind": "inherited_unit",
      "polarity": "SUPPORTED",
      "value": "`Aspose.Imaging.Foss` identifies an image's format and reads its basic properties\n(dimensions, bit depth, frame count) directly from the file header \u2014 without\ndecoding a single pixel. It's built for cases where you need to know **what**\na file is and **how big** it is, fast, without pulling in a full imaging stack."
    },
    {
      "attributes": {
        "section": "Aspose.Imaging FOSS for .NET"
      },
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "detail": "lines 14-14; paragraph; under Aspose.Imaging FOSS for .NET",
          "path": "README.md"
        }
      ],
      "id": "inherited_unit:005.paragraph",
      "kind": "inherited_unit",
      "polarity": "SUPPORTED",
      "value": "It has no NuGet dependencies and targets `netstandard2.0` and `net8.0`."
    },
    {
      "attributes": {
        "section": "Aspose.Imaging FOSS for .NET"
      },
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "detail": "lines 16-16; heading; under Aspose.Imaging FOSS for .NET",
          "path": "README.md"
        }
      ],
      "id": "inherited_unit:006.heading",
      "kind": "inherited_unit",
      "polarity": "SUPPORTED",
      "value": "## Why this exists"
    },
    {
      "attributes": {
        "section": "Aspose.Imaging FOSS for .NET > Why this exists"
      },
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "detail": "lines 18-21; paragraph; under Aspose.Imaging FOSS for .NET > Why this exists",
          "path": "README.md"
        }
      ],
      "id": "inherited_unit:007.paragraph",
      "kind": "inherited_unit",
      "polarity": "SUPPORTED",
      "value": "Most .NET image libraries make you fully decode an image just to answer \"is\nthis a JPEG, and how big is it?\". `ImageSharp.Image.Identify` covers common\nraster formats well, but nothing in the .NET FOSS ecosystem does the same for\nPSD, EMF/WMF, or DICOM. This library covers that full range in one place."
    },
    {
      "attributes": {
        "section": "Aspose.Imaging FOSS for .NET > Why this exists"
      },
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "detail": "lines 23-25; paragraph; under Aspose.Imaging FOSS for .NET > Why this exists",
          "path": "README.md"
        }
      ],
      "id": "inherited_unit:008.paragraph",
      "kind": "inherited_unit",
      "polarity": "SUPPORTED",
      "value": "If you need to actually **decode, edit, or convert** any of these formats,\nthat's a different job \u2014 see [Aspose.Imaging](https://products.aspose.com/imaging/net/)\nfor a full-featured commercial SDK covering all of these formats and more."
    },
    {
      "attributes": {
        "section": "Aspose.Imaging FOSS for .NET"
      },
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "evidence": [
        {
